what's going on guys let's talk suicide  squad  the suicide squad movie was really fun  it was a really really really good movie  here's the funny thing though  i see a lot of people out there who are  vocalizing complaints and kind of  comparing it to the marvel cinematic  universe thing  there's not really a lot of character  development going on there there's a  reason for that  if you are familiar with the suicide  squad comics you know that james gunn  nailed the movie and the reason for that  is sure rick flagg and harley quinn got  a lot of screen time and we already knew  who they were we knew that they were  basically going to make it into the end  for the rest of the cast bloodsport and  king shark and polkadot man all that  kind of stuff  we didn't really get a whole lot of  backstory there i mean we did to a  degree where we got  kind of an origin for polkadot in the  sense of like he's the result of his  mom's experimentation and some of his  brothers and sisters lived  others died he's got to spew out those  polka dots twice a day otherwise they'll  consume him alive  so we got really more explanation on his  story than we did pretty much anybody  else but you got what amounts to like  quick little explanations right amanda  waller said that bloodsport basically  put superman  in the icu with a kryptonite bullet and  then the most we get outside of that is  like  the relationship between himself and his  daughter is pretty straight right we  don't even really get an origin for king  shark  but it's one of these things where you  don't really get a whole lot going there  and there's a reason for that so the  suicide squad in dc comics is designed  to be  in effect a throwaway team and dc uses  the suicide squad for a couple of  different reasons  one is to sometimes boost the popularity  of villains that exist in the dc  landscape  because the team has really been popular  since harley quinn was put on it  which makes sense because nobody would  care about suicide squad if harley quinn  wasn't on it  or the other reason why they use it is  to get rid of villains right to write  them out here's a really good example  in recent years dc comics created a  character named punchline who was  designed to replace harley quinn  no it didn't work nobody cares so what  you'll likely see  is that punchline will be rolled over  into the suicide squad relatively soon  and then she'll die like three or four  issues after her first appearance  if not maybe 10 or so right but she'll  die within two story arcs  because dc is just writing her character  out and when she's dead you'll never see  her hear from her again  that's what they end up using it for but  the entire basis behind the suicide  squad is with the exception of harley  quinn in the comics  is designed to be a rotating roster that  the villains who are on the team  don't really matter because they're  designed to be cannon fodder  and james gunn nailed that with this  movie it's why when the movie opens up  literally the first team that you think  is a suicide squad dies  which admittedly i wish michael rooker  had more time in that film  and now that i think about it james gunn  if you see this video  i really hope we get a prequel to the  suicide squad that takes place between  the terrible one that had will smith  and this great one that you made that  basically gives us like adventures  with the first team that died in the  very beginning because i kind of want to  see that  i really want to see a movie with that  team it looked amazing right like  disconnecting man or whatever his name  is  i really want to see that but the  important thing here is that's why you  didn't really get a whole lot of  development in relation to the villains  because literally the next suicide squad  movie could open up and idris elba dies  in the first five minutes that's just  the nature of the team anybody can die  at any point in time under virtually any  circumstance they're designed to be  throwaway  having said that with regards to pretty  much everything else in the movie  it was fantastic it's exactly what i was  hoping it would be a comic book film  composed of super villains that didn't  take itself too seriously  i think the biggest issue with the first  suicide squad film is it didn't feel  like that it felt like they were trying  to make like this real  tangible amazing comic book movie that  was in line with something like the  marvel cinematic universe  and that's not really what the suicide  squad is supposed to be it's supposed to  be a movie about villains who can die at  any point in time  and who cares the story is what's  important  not really the characters and james gunn  nailed that the story was great  i am kind of shocked that they use  starro  as the main villain if i'm being honest  starro was a justice league villain  right that was like the first big thing  for the justice league  was fighting starro so i always kind of  hoped that starro would be a villain  that justice lee would face off against  having said that  starro does seem kind of goofy and kind  of silly and he is  currently in dc comics he's in a jar so  he's called jaro literally he hangs out  with batman all the time  but it's one of those things where it's  kind of like that's kind of goofy and  silly so  maybe staro really was a great fit for  the suicide squad because it worked  right it was cool  it was kind of sad at the end right when  like starro died he was like  i was just i was happy just floating in  space staring at the stars  and then humanity came along and screwed  it up i feel like that's james gunn's  just critique on humanity like hey guys  what's one thing humanity's really good  at screwing stuff up  awesome because we are we're really good  at screwing things up  but that's that's kind of the craziness  about it right you know it's the movie  was  fun it was it was enjoyable it was a  great popcorn film  i don't know that i would go and see it  again and that's really kind of  the interesting thing about it a lot of  people really determine whether or not  they consider a movie to be good  by whether or not they would go and see  it a second time i saw infinity war in  avengers in-game once that was enough  for me right i mean i was like this is  cool  not gonna go see it again so that's not  really my standard for determining  whether or not a movie is good but i  know some of you guys use that standard  so i figured i would go ahead and impart  that on you having said that for my  standard  did i have a good time was i ever bored  did i find myself yawning over the  course of the movie that's kind of my  standard  if i yawn in the movie and i'm not  really exhausted  then it's like your movie sucks and it's  boring right like the irishman i fell  asleep during that movie  twice that movie was bad it was bad and  it was boring  i'm sorry martin scorsese you peaked  with goodfellas but the important thing  here  is that with a suicide squad film it was  great it was fun it was enjoyable right  it's one of those movies you can just  kind of go  and just have a good time just watch  some crazy stuff happen i did love the  hyper violence  that's one of the things that i really  did enjoy i feel like there wasn't  really enough  like dark humor comedic like hyper  violence  like there was you know in in the first  movie i mean the first movie sure there  was violence but it was more like  like typical violence right like  standard comic book violence right like  i mean i will say that like like was it  deadshot like shooting up all those  those zombie monster things that was  like the only good part of the whole  movie literally  you guys you guys agree i've seen how  many views that video has on youtube  everybody loves that scene right it's  one of the coolest scenes nobody  cares about any of the other scenes in  that movie but the cool thing is is with  this film it's just it's enjoyable it's  good right so  if what you're looking for is something  that doesn't feel like the marvel  cinematic universe in the sense that  it doesn't feel a cookie cutter  formulaic it's kind of a breakaway  small hints of guardians of the galaxy  in there chris pratt did have a cameo i  wonder if you guys spotted it  uh small little things like that in  there it's good it's it's just  it's separate and it's unique and it's  interesting it's fun  and i really believe that james gunn's  portrayal of the suicide squad in this  movie is almost kind of like his  guardians of the galaxy thing right like  i can take a ridiculously obscure team  that you didn't even know existed until  we announced the movie and i bet i can  turn it into like a huge hit again  that's the big difference  the entire guardians of the galaxy film  got a lot of character development  suicide squad didn't right it was more  about the story so you probably walk  away  more curious about starro or any or  maybe probably king shark king shark was  the best character in the whole movie  let's all just  admit that but like you know you might  walk away with more of a curiosity about  starro and king shark than anybody else  but the story is what you likely  remember the most because  that's the main emphasis of suicide  squad so i i love that right i mean i  think that this movie shows  that dc has great characters they've got  great characters that you can do a lot  of stuff with their characters  all you need is a competent director all  you need is somebody who can come along  and say hey  i can make great movies with these  characters right and you're not gonna  have to get a special cut in order for  that to happen so with that being said  guys we're going to bring this to an end  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

