igned to be  throwaway  having said that with regards to pretty  much everything else in the movie  it was fantastic it's exactly what i was  hoping it would be a comic book film  composed of super villains that didn't  take itself too seriously  i think the biggest issue with the first  suicide squad film is it didn't feel  like that it felt like they were trying  to make like this real  tangible amazing comic book movie that  was in line with something like the  marvel cinematic universe  and that's not really what the suicide  squad is supposed to be it's supposed to  be a movie about villains who can die at  any point in time  and who cares the story is what's  important  not really the characters and james gunn  nailed that the story was great  i am kind of shocked that they use  starro  as the main villain if i'm being honest  starro was a justice league villain  right that was like the first big thing  for the justice league  was fighting starro so i always kind of  hoped that starro would be a villain  that justice lee would face off against  having said that  starro does seem kind of goofy and kind  of silly and he is  currently in dc comics he's in a jar so  he's called jaro literally he hangs out  with batman all the time  but it's one of those things where it's  kind of like that's kind of goofy and  silly so  maybe staro really was a great fit for  the suicide squad because it worked  right it was cool  it was kind of sad at the end right when  like starro died he was like  i was just i was happy just floating in  space staring at the stars  and then humanity came along and screwed  it up i feel like that's james gunn's  just critique on humanity like hey guys  what's one thing humanity's really good  at screwing stuff up  awesome because we are we're really good  at screwing things up  but that's that's kind of the craziness  about it right you know it's the movie  was  fun it was it was enjoyable it was a  great popcorn film  i don't know that i would go and see it  again and that's really kind of  the interesting thing about it a lot of  people really determine whether or not  they consider a movie to be good  by whether or not they would go and see  it a second time i saw infinity war in  avengers in-game once that was enough  for me right i mean i was like this is  cool  not gonna go see it again so that's not  really my standard for determining  whether or not a movie is good but i  know some of you guys use that standard  so i figured i would go ahead and impart  that on you having said that for my  standard  did i have a good time was i ever bored  did i find myself yawning over the  course of the movie that's kind of my  standard  if i yawn in the movie and i'm not  really exhausted  then it's like your movie sucks and it's  boring right like the irishman i fell  asleep during that movie  twice that movie was bad it was bad and  it was boring  i'm sorry martin scorsese you peaked  with goodfellas but the important thing  here  is that with a suicide squad film it was  great it was fun it was enjoyable right  it's one of those movies you can just  kind of go  and just have a good time just watch  some crazy stuff happen i did love the  hyper violence  that's one of the things that i really  did enjoy i feel like there wasn't  really enough  like dark humor comedic like hyper  violence  like there was you know in in the first  movie i mean the first movie sure there  was violence but it was more like  like typical violence right like  standard comic book violence right like  i mean i will say that like like was it  deadshot like shooting up all those  those zombie monster things that was  like the only good part of the whole  movie literally  you guys you guys agree i've seen how  many views that video has on youtube  everybody loves that scene right it's  one of the coolest scenes nobody  cares about any of the other scenes in  that movie but the cool thing is is with  this film it's just it's enjoyable it's  good right so  if what you're looking for is something  that doesn't feel like the marvel  cinematic universe in the sense that  it doesn't feel a cookie cutter  formulaic it's kind of a breakaway  small hints of guardians of the galaxy  in there chris pratt did have a cameo i  wonder if you guys spotted it  uh small little things like that in  there it's good it's it's just  it's separate and it's unique and it's  interesting it's fun  and i really believe that james gunn's  portrayal of the suicide squad in this  movie is almost kind of like his  guardians of the galaxy thing right like  i can take a ridiculously obscure team  that you didn't even know existed until  we announced the movie and i bet i can  turn it into like a huge hit again  that's the big difference  the entire guardians of the galaxy film  got a lot of character development  suicide squad didn't right it was more  about the story so you probably walk  away  more curious about starro or any or  maybe probably king shark king shark was  the best character in the whole movie  let's all just  admit that but like you know you might  walk away with more of a curiosity about  starro and king shark than anybody else  but the story is what you likely  remember the most because  that's the main emphasis of suicide  squad so i i love that right i mean i  think that this movie shows  that dc has great characters they've got  great characters that you can do a lot  of stuff with their characters  all you need is a competent director all  you need is somebody who can come along  and say hey  i can make great movies with these  characters right and you're not gonna  have to get a special cut in order for  that to happen so with that being said  guys we're going to bring this to an end  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace


